<title>BELGIUM: Export refund cut only on non-tender products - EU.</title>
<headline>Export refund cut only on non-tender products - EU.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on on Friday  that its decision to cut export refunds by 5 percent only applied  for products on which it does nor call for tender.</p>
<p>Clarifying an earlier statement by a spokesman, the Commission said  its cut does not apply to cereals because there are no calls for tender.  Cereals are dealt with when requests come in.</p>
<p>The spokesman earlier said the 5 percent cut had been made &quot;for all  products across the board.&quot; It was triggered by the rise in the dollar.</p>
<p>--BRUSSELS +32 2 287-6830</p>
</text>
